	Context Switching is the process of saving the state (context) of a currently running process or thread and loading the state of another process or thread so that CPU execution can switch between them.
	
What is "Context"?
	The context is all the information needed to resume execution later.
	
It includes:

	Program Counter (PC)
	CPU Registers
	Stack Pointer
	Process State
	Scheduling Information
	
